:[],"text":"Set \\(p=u_x,\\ q=u_y\\) and \\(F=pq-u\\). Charpit’s equations are\n\\[\n\\dot x=F_p=q,\\qquad \\dot y=F_q=p,\\qquad\n\\dot u=pF_p+qF_q=2pq,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\dot p=-F_x-pF_u=p,\\qquad\n\\dot q=-F_y-qF_u=q.\n\\]\n\nAt \\(s=0\\), the initial data give\n\\[\nx=0,\\quad y=\\tau,\\quad u=\\tau^2.\n\\]\nDifferentiating along the initial curve yields \\(q_0=2\\tau\\). Thus \\(p_0q_0=u_0\\) gives \\(p_0=\\tau/2\\) for \\(\\tau\\ne0\\), with the same value at \\(\\tau=0\\) by smooth continuation. (At that single point, the initial relation alone does not determine \\(p_0\\).)\n\nConsequently,\n\\[\np=\\frac{\\tau}{2}e^s,\\qquad q=2\\tau e^s.\n\\]\nIntegrating the remaining equations with the initial values,\n\\[\nx=2\\tau(e^s-1),\\qquad\ny=\\tau+\\frac{\\tau}{2}(e^s-1)=\\frac{\\tau}{2}(e^s+1),\n\\qquad\nu=\\tau^2e^{2s}.\n\\]\nThese satisfy \\(pq=u\\) and the prescribed initial curve for every real \\(\\tau\\).\n\nFinal answer: **Option 3:** \\(\\displaystyle x=2\\tau(e^s-1),\\quad y=\\frac{\\tau}{2}(e^s+1),\\quad u=\\tau^2e^{2s}\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":371,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":562,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":171},"total_tokens":933},"user":null,"metadata":{}}
